1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,855
The evidence meeting took an hour and was held in a local office with a door onto the street.

2
00:00:04,855 --> 00:00:13,639
At the middle of the table lay a solar lamp, an experimental sock, and a brass bolt from a hospital hatch.

3
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:18,013
“Take the metric seriously,” the doctor said.

4
00:00:18,013 --> 00:00:29,537
“A centimeter on a knee is a kilometer on a career.” A car brought two more people from the area, and the business of the day began.

5
00:00:29,537 --> 00:00:37,495
The heritage of the district was a prejudice about bodies: a productive worker, a marginal patient.

6
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:42,565
“Send the forecast to the local industry,” Maya said.

7
00:00:42,565 --> 00:00:54,233
“Exclusion is not a precaution.” A bolt of sunlight through the window fell on the toe of a boot, and the watchful nurse wrote down the hour.

8
00:00:54,233 --> 00:01:00,627
The progression of the disease was reversible if the dependence on the nail of a habit was broken.

9
00:01:00,627 --> 00:01:07,306
“Underneath the obesity there is a drunkard's punctuality,” the physiotherapist said.

10
00:01:07,306 --> 00:01:20,079
“Periodic fasting, fertile soil, and a refinement of the diet — that is all I ask.” The deadliest thing on the table was the inside of the ledger.

11
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:30,058
They measured the foot, the knee, and the sock in millimeters and centimeters, and compared the numbers with the fertility of the club's own records.

12
00:01:30,058 --> 00:01:34,092
“Bring the small ones,” the doctor said.

13
00:01:34,092 --> 00:01:50,510
“A centimeter is a warning, a millimeter is a fact.” An affluence of nourishment and an inferiority of sleep: the drunkard in the corner had understood it before any of them, and the habit had become the whole question.

14
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:58,189
The alert on the machine was followed by a second alert, and then by a period of quiet.

15
00:01:58,189 --> 00:02:05,038
The forecast for the season was poor, and the team had to hospitalize nobody that month.

16
00:02:05,038 --> 00:02:24,665
“About the span of a life,” the doctor said, “a body is the only country we all live in.” A pedestrian in a car, a shop on the road, and a place by the door: the evidence, at last, was about people who had never been in the room.

17
00:02:24,665 --> 00:02:36,418
About the area, the business, and the local industry, the evidence was clear: a country that sends its workers home by car is not a country that walks.

18
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:44,532
The office by the door, the road outside, and the street beyond it were all part of the same measurement.

19
00:02:44,532 --> 00:02:52,460
“Make it a habit,” the doctor said, “and take the use of the place seriously.”
